  "page": {
    "lede": "Every announced show the updater could find for the next 12 months, from the Saddledome and the Jubilee down to the Palomino, the King Eddy, the Blues Can and the church-hall folk series. Star the shows you want, narrow by date, area, genre or price, and copy any list straight into Excel or your calendar.",
    "caveats": [
      "This list is rebuilt from Songkick, Eventbrite, Showpass, Live Nation venue pages and (when a key is set) the Ticketmaster API. Shows found once stay on the list until their date passes, so a show cancelled quietly at the source can linger. Check the linked page before you buy.",
      "Venue sites that load their calendars by script (the Palace, Grey Eagle's own site, Werklund Centre, the Blues Can, the Calgary Phil, MRU tickets) are not read automatically. Shows from those venues come from the original October 2026 research, from the aggregators above, or from rows you add to data\\manual.tsv.",
      "Clubs and bars usually announce only 1 to 3 months ahead, so later months fill in as the year goes on. Festival lineups (Stampede, Folk Fest, Sled Island) show up once they are announced.",
      "\"May be cancelled\" means a show in the next 90 days that the listing sites used to show but has been missing from the last two complete refreshes. It is a prompt to check, not a confirmed cancellation.",
      "Times and prices come from Showpass, Ticketmaster and the venue's own wording where they give them; many listings have neither. Prices are ticket prices before fees."
    ]
  }
